title: Veeam: Restore points
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the restore points of a machine (e.g. a virtual
 machine) backed up by a Veeam Backup & Replication server, collected via
 the Veeam special agent. It reports the age of the last restore point, the
 number of restore points, the platform, the object type, the type of the
 last restore point and the malware status.

 This check is {CRIT} if the object has no restore point at all, since it
 cannot be recovered. It is {UNKNOWN} if the last restore point is not
 found. {WARN} and {CRIT} levels can be set for the age of the last restore
 point (default: 30 and 48 hours).

 The malware status is the worst one across all restore points of the
 object: {OK} if clean or informative, {WARN} if suspicious, {CRIT} if
 infected and {UNKNOWN} for any other value. This mapping is not
 configurable.

discovery:
 One service is created on each backed up machine, delivered via piggyback
 to the host named after the machine's name in its Veeam backup chain (the
 same host that receives the Veeam backup services). A machine backed up
 by several jobs, or by several Veeam servers, gets one service for all of
 them.
